    <briefdescription>
<para>This class implements a wrapper to the Spectra generalized eigen solver for square real symmetric matrices, i.e. to solve <formula id="79">$ Ax = \lambda Bx$</formula>, where A is symmetric and B is positive definite. It calculates a selection of eigenvalues. At most <formula id="81">$ n - 1 $</formula>, where <formula id="82">$ n $</formula> is the number of rows/cols of the matrices. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Under the hood it uses the Spectra::SymGEigsSolver with Cholesky decomposition for B</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>MT</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>the used Matrix Type, can be a sparse or dense Eigen::Matrix </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
